  "summary": "I reconciled all four medication lists per RBC-TOC-02 and wrote a reconciliation note in each chart. Five items need your decision: Walter Kim's lisinopril, Terence Stark's glipizide and atorvastatin, Adelaide Thompson's levothyroxine and Earnest Roberts's sertraline.\n\n**Walter Kim** (pt-0005; note doc-t0004)\n- **Furosemide:** changed to 40 mg twice daily, per the signed addendum. It overrides the summary's 40 mg daily. New order mr-t0001.\n- **Potassium chloride:** stopped (mr-00076), per the discharge summary.\n- **Pantoprazole:** not ordered. It was an inpatient formulary substitution, so he stays on his home omeprazole.\n- **Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin:** unchanged.\n- **For you — lisinopril stays on hold (mr-00072).** The discharge condition is met: creatinine was 1.32 on the 10/21 outside lab, below the 1.5 cutoff. But potassium on that panel was 5.4, above the policy's 5.0 limit. I created task-t0003 for you, due 10/26, to decide once his next potassium is back.\n\n**Terence Stark** (pt-0004; note doc-t0008)\n- **Carvedilol (Coreg):** increased to 12.5 mg twice daily (new order mr-t0005).\n- **Aspirin and insulin 70/30 at 18 units twice daily:** unchanged.\n- **For you — atorvastatin 80 mg (mr-00055):** the discharge continues it, but it was last filled 3/4/2026. That covers only about 24% of the 180 days before admission, below the 80% threshold. I left it unchanged and messaged you (comm-t0006).\n- **For you — glipizide 5 mg:** an outside endocrinologist (Dr. Desai) prescribes it and it's being filled regularly. There is no clinic order, and the discharge summary doesn't mention it. I did not order it and messaged you urgently (comm-t0007), since he is also on insulin and has stage 3 CKD (hypoglycemia risk).\n\n**Adelaide Thompson** (pt-0042; note doc-t0012)\n- **Nifedipine ER (Procardia XL):** increased to 60 mg daily (new order mr-t0009).\n- **Hydrochlorothiazide:** stopped (mr-00362). The signed addendum says stop and do not restart, because it caused her hyponatremia. This overrides the summary's \"continue.\"\n- **For you — levothyroxine 100 mcg (mr-00360):** the discharge continues it, but fills cover only about 41% of the 180 days before admission, and her inpatient TSH was 7.9. I left it unchanged and messaged you (comm-t0011).\n\n**Earnest Roberts** (pt-0044; note doc-t0015)\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg:** restarted the held order (mr-00373). The discharge condition is met: creatinine was 1.08 on the 10/22 outside lab, below the 1.3 cutoff. Potassium on that panel was 4.6. His 10/20 potassium had been 5.3.\n- **Atorvastatin:** not ordered. It was an inpatient formulary substitution, so he stays on his home rosuvastatin 10 mg.\n- **Glargine and lispro insulin:** unchanged.\n- **For you — sertraline 100 mg:** an outside psychiatrist (Dr. Nair) prescribes it. There is no clinic order, and the discharge summary doesn't mention it. I did not order it and messaged you (comm-t0014).",
